Carafe: SuspendThread pauses a Windows thread and TerminateThread ends it.
A started thread without the ARM64EC doorbell is paused by the kernel (svcSetThreadActivity) when it is in
PE code, and its registers come from svcGetThreadContext3. In the runtime's own code it may hold a lock,
so it gets a stop request instead and stops at its next system call, sleep or wait. A thread parked in a
wait without registers is read the same way. TerminateThread sets an end request: the thread ends itself
at its next system call, its waits return STATUS_THREAD_IS_TERMINATING, and an exception it takes
ends it (FEX frees a thread's state before it is terminated).
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

